{"In testCacheIDPForLogin, getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(\"alias\")::remove) uses the hardcoded literal \"alias\" instead of the actual created alias (e.g. \"idp-alias-0\"), making all cleanup callbacks ineffective and leaking test data across tests": 0.9350663423538208, "In remove(String alias), the code fetches the stored identity provider by alias without checking if the result is null, then calls registerIDPInvalidation(storedIdp) which will throw a NullPointerException if storedIdp is null since it immediately dereferences it to call idp.getInternalId() and idp.getAlias()": 0.861815333366394, "The getLoginPredicate was changed to include organization public-check which may not map exactly to per-mode getForLogin behavior since the predicate is used globally for cache invalidation decisions and does not take FetchMode into account, potentially causing behavioral divergence": 0.3541337251663208}